"date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T19:37:43-07:00","id":1447882,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that's now in my podcast queue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T05:05:42-07:00","id":1447929,"title":"","content":"Oh, neat stuff. Thanks for sharing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T14:02:07-07:00","id":1447984,"title":"","content":"I am listening to it, and let me say something: I am all for having a simpler system for player exalted, but I don't want to make all exalted types have the same power level.<br /> <br /> Is there a simple way to recreate the usual power gradient between exalted types?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T19:50:27-07:00","id":1448010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1447984#post1447984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am listening to it, and let me say something: I am all for having a simpler system for player exalted, but I don't want to make all exalted types have the same power level.<br /> <br /> Is there a simple way to recreate the usual power gradient between exalted types?</div> </div> </div> </div>Until we have a more complete picture of the rules, I don't think there's currently any such suggestion. ANd it also depends greatly on how much of the gradient you want to be there. Remember that as they note, there is some areas that Exalts are stornger and Solars are pretty upfront the most strategically capable ones as per the podcast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T07:46:50-07:00","id":1448045,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I thought there would be playtesters, I saw that there was a lot of discussion about Essence, I didn't keep up.<br /> <br /> Enough to make them a credible menace to the age, I think. That depends on what is strategic, are they the Military General Exalted types now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T09:55:15-07:00","id":1448051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448045#post1448045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I thought there would be playtesters, I saw that there was a lot of discussion about Essence, I didn't keep up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is mostly about the podcast recently. So more info can be found there, including what their goals on power are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448045#post1448045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enough to make them a credible menace to the age, I think. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do this without having other Exalts pay more xp for worse Charms. Especially in the case where in 3e to start and Essence for sure, most NPCs are not fully-statted characters using PC rules, so are as powerful or not as needed for the game.<br /> <br /> Solars are more a threat due to individual capabilities, competence, and unique things that they can do that others can't easily or quickly. There's more to power than just indivdiual combat prowess. ANd in this case Solars I thinks till are strongest?<br /> <br /> They're also a threat in the current age since isntead of like ten reincarnating every few years, there's nearly three hundred of them and thier derivitives aorund while the main polity that kept Anathema in check is about to go to civil war. There's a lot that can make Solars upending powers without that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448045#post1448045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That depends on what is strategic, are they the Military General Exalted types now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strategic in a game systems sense, not in-setting military sense. Solars have more broad options to approach things than other Exalts. Their Advantages, Modes, and Charms tend to be more consistently applicable, while they have the broadest access to &quot;shared&quot; stuff like sorcery, necromancy, martial arts, and Evocations.<br /> <br /> Strategies are ways you achieve your goals in something. Solars have by their braod applicablity of power more strategic options than other Exalts due to general comptence of execution.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T12:10:10-07:00","id":1448059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448051#post1448051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is mostly about the podcast recently. So more info can be found there, including what their goals on power are.<br /> <br /> <br /> They can do this without having other Exalts pay more xp for worse Charms. Especially in the case where in 3e to start and Essence for sure, most NPCs are not fully-statted characters using PC rules, so are as powerful or not as needed for the game.<br /> <br /> Solars are more a threat due to individual capabilities, competence, and unique things that they can do that others can't easily or quickly. There's more to power than just indivdiual combat prowess. ANd in this case Solars I thinks till are strongest?<br /> <br /> They're also a threat in the current age since isntead of like ten reincarnating every few years, there's nearly three hundred of them and thier derivitives aorund while the main polity that kept Anathema in check is about to go to civil war. There's a lot that can make Solars upending powers without that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to thread-dump any more to make this a discussion of the validity of what I said. I just would like to know if there was a way to make to way *I* think it's better, for my own motives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strategic in a game systems sense, not in-setting military sense. Solars have more broad options to approach things than other Exalts. Their Advantages, Modes, and Charms tend to be more consistently applicable, while they have the broadest access to &quot;shared&quot; stuff like sorcery, necromancy, martial arts, and Evocations.<br /> <br /> Strategies are ways you achieve your goals in something. Solars have by their braod applicablity of power more strategic options than other Exalts due to general comptence of execution. </div> </div> </div>So not strategic in as a 'nuke', strategic in as an all-terrain vehicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T19:10:50-07:00","id":1448088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448059#post1448059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to thread-dump any more to make this a discussion of the validity of what I said. I just would like to know if there was a way to make to way *I* think it's better, for my own motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno. It's not the goal of the writers, so you'll have to see what hte final product is and make that decison/start a thread likely on the topic when we have more to work on than the hints so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T04:52:46-07:00","id":1448117,"title":"","content":"Great podcast! Thanks for sharing buddy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26776-cornelgo","name":"cornelGo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T08:26:22-07:00","id":1448129,"title":"","content":"Listening to this episode did NOT help my overly excited impatience.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://tenor.com/L4jU.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T15:48:04-07:00","id":1448362,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly one of Solars\u2019 Advantages is literally \u201cFree full excellencies on everything\u201d which is WHOAH as far as staying on top of the heap goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T19:24:29-07:00","id":1448377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448362#post1448362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand correctly one of Solars\u2019 Advantages is literally \u201cFree full excellencies on everything\u201d which is WHOAH as far as staying on top of the heap goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellencies that they <i>have,</i> yeah, but thus far I dunno that we've seen enough to know whether Solars are back to buying excellencies or what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T06:44:14-07:00","id":1448416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1447877-exalted-essence-in-onyx-podcast?p=1448377#post1448377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellencies that they <i>have,</i> yeah, but thus far I dunno that we've seen enough to know whether Solars are back to buying excellencies or what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars still have to buy Excellencies post-chargen (or pick them up when they rise in Essence). It's also worth noting that they don't pay for the Charm invocation of an Excellency, but they still must invoke it; if they want to use another Charm on Step 1 instead, they have to choose between that and their Excellency.<br /> <br /> But yeah - in their areas of competence Solars consistently have a dice advantage that they get totally free, all the time. And if you manage to tie with them, they win, even if you're the defender.<br /> <br /> Abyssals and Infernals both have Advantages that give them either a once-per-scene refresh on motes or a bonus to mote regeneration when they do certain things, which roughly maths out to &quot;what you'd get for not having to pay for those Excellencies you're throwing around&quot;. Parity between Solars and Solar-derivatives was still a big thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T15:36:34-07:00","id":1448474,"title":"","content":"At last! I'm happy for this podcast!<br /> <br /> Soon... the GIBBENNING WILL BE AT HAND!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T23:26:51-07:00","id":1448658,"title":"","content":"I am cautiously optimistic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T18:02:50-07:00","id":1448734,"title":"","content":"Great episode! Exalted Essence is already on my &quot;must buy&quot; list and I am prepping myself with Exalted lore to run the game. The 3E core book is quite good but it's tough to convince a group to try it out. It's intimidating. I am hoping EE is the door through which I convince my group to give this wonderful game a try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T19:45:55-07:00","id":1448825,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to the alchemicals. As I understand it, most setting background will still be in the various splatbooks for spaces sake, but given that the alchemical book is so far out, I'm hoping for at least a few pages explaining how they exist in Creation.<br /> Because I want my Robo-kung-fu sage, wandering the highways and byways of creation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T21:00:06-07:00","id":1449509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.th